  "id": "aboriginal_country_music",
  "name": "Aboriginal country music (Koori and Murri country)",
  "family": "country",
  "lineage": "Country and gospel-country song made by Aboriginal singers on missions and reserves and in country towns from the mid-twentieth century, drawing on hillbilly records and radio and on a strong local voice-and-guitar tradition. Recorded artists include Jimmy Little, born at Cummeragunja, whose Royal Telephone was a 1963 hit, Dougie Young, Vic Simms, Harry Williams and the Country Outcasts and Roger Knox; Clinton Walker's book, CD compilation and film Buried Country (2000) documented the tradition.",
  "recipe": "classic early-1960s aboriginal country music, functional Song, country branch. dreadnought acoustic single coil electric guitar, electric bass, drum kit. treated studio. tube condenser, 500-series boutique pre, brick-wall limiter, dynamic EQ. 24-bit digital plate reverb digital delay pitch shifter.",
